; Your first part in loon
; =======================
;
; This file is the part. Open it in any text editor, change a number, save,
; and vcad rebuilds the model on screen. Make a mistake and the error shows
; up with its line number; the last good model stays put until you fix it.
;
; Units are millimetres. Z is up.

; 1. Dimensions you'll want to change later are parameters. They show up in
;    the inspector, so you can also drag them there.
[defparam width 60.0 :unit "mm" :min 30 :max 120]
[defparam depth 40.0 :unit "mm" :min 20 :max 80]
[defparam thick 6.0 :unit "mm" :min 2 :max 12]
[defparam hole 4.0 :unit "mm" :min 2 :max 8]

; 2. A plate: a box from the origin out to (width, depth, thick), with its
;    edges rounded. Operations take the shape LAST: [fillet radius shape].
[let plate [fillet 1.0 [cube width depth thick]]]

; 3. One mounting hole: a cylinder (radius, height) along Z, taller than the
;    plate so it cuts all the way through.
[let drill [cylinder [/ hole 2] [* thick 3]]]

; 4. Put a hole near each corner. `translate` takes x y z, then the shape.
[let inset 8.0]
[let holes
  [union [translate inset inset -1 drill]
  [union [translate [- width inset] inset -1 drill]
  [union [translate inset [- depth inset] -1 drill]
         [translate [- width inset] [- depth inset] -1 drill]]]]]

; 5. Cut the holes out of the plate: [difference tool shape] is
;    "shape minus tool".
[let drilled [difference holes plate]]

; 6. Tell vcad this is a part, and what it's made of.
[root drilled "aluminum"]

; Try it:
;   - change `width` to 90 and save
;   - add a boss:  [root [translate 30 20 thick [cylinder 8 10]] "aluminum"]
;   - misspell `plate` as `plat` and save, then fix it
